|* Post-layout ro_array_core (whole array, real inter-ring wiring), FLOATING
|* substrate, rings 2-4 PRESENT BUT STOPPED (en2/en3/en4 held at 0 for the
|* whole run) -- the array-scale sibling of
|* sim/post-layout-ro-ring5/testbench/tb_post_layout_substrate_float_solo.spice.
|*
|* Purpose: separate LOADING (the floating node's own capacitance/impedance,
|* present even with no other ring switching) from COUPLING (ring 1's period
|* moving because rings 2-4 are actually driving the same shared node), the
|* same three-way decomposition DR-0005 finding 3 used at ring scope:
|*
|*   loading  = t(this deck)                         - t(tied, sibling deck)
|*   coupling = t(substrate_float, all 4 running)     - t(this deck)
|*
|* Same array GDS extraction as the other two decks in this directory (real
|* physical ring-to-ring proximity, not four separately-placed leaf cells),
|* so this is the strongest available bound on the substrate mechanism this
|* repo has produced -- still not the physical answer (the extractor emits
|* no substrate or tap resistance at all; klayout-tools#1503), but bracketing
|* the terminals of a real, physically-placed layout's own shared node
|* rather than a hand-tied approximation of one.
|*
|* With en2/en3/en4 held at 0, ro_nand2's own defined-output-on-disable state
|* (design/README.md; DR-0003) pins ring2/3/4's node ro_ring5 outputs high --
|* a defined, non-switching state, not a floating one -- so rn2/rn3/rn4 (and
|* therefore ro2/ro3/ro4 and the XOR tree downstream of them) settle and stay
|* put; only ring 1 free-runs.
|*
|* This file is a TEMPLATE: sim/bin/corner-run.py substitutes /Users/rwalters/.volare/volare/sky130/versions/c6d73a35f524070e85faff4a6a9eef49553ebc2b/sky130A/libs.tech/combined/sky130.lib.spice,
|* ff, /Users/rwalters/GitHub/sky130-trng/.loom/worktrees/issue-22/layout/pex-array/ro_array_core_pex.spice, -40.0 and 1.62. As committed it is not a
|* runnable deck. Invoke with
|* `--pex-lib layout/pex-array/ro_array_core_pex.spice`.
|
|.option scale=1u
|.lib "/Users/rwalters/.volare/volare/sky130/versions/c6d73a35f524070e85faff4a6a9eef49553ebc2b/sky130A/libs.tech/combined/sky130.lib.spice" ff
|
|.include "/Users/rwalters/GitHub/sky130-trng/.loom/worktrees/issue-22/layout/pex-array/ro_array_core_pex.spice"
|
|.temp -40.0
|
|* --- substrate return node: FLOATING (see header) -- no Vsub source ----
|
|Vddrp1 pvddr1 0 dc 1.62
|Vddrp2 pvddr2 0 dc 1.62
|Vddrp3 pvddr3 0 dc 1.62
|Vddrp4 pvddr4 0 dc 1.62
|Vddp pvdd 0 dc 1.62
|Venp1 pen1 0 PULSE(0 1.62 5n 100p 100p 1u 2u)
|* rings 2-4: held at 0 for the whole run -- present, but never released.
|Venp2 pen2 0 dc 0
|Venp3 pen3 0 dc 0
|Venp4 pen4 0 dc 0
|xarr pen1 pen2 pen3 pen4 pvddr1 pvddr2 pvddr3 pvddr4 pvdd 0 pxo pro1 pro2 pro3 pro4 ro_array_core_pex
|
|.ic v(pro1)=0
|.ic v(pro2)=0
|.ic v(pro3)=0
|.ic v(pro4)=0
|
|.save v(pro1) v(xarr.vsubs)
|.save i(Vddrp1)
|
|.tran 5p 800n uic
|
|.control
|run
|
|meas tran pt1a when v(pro1)=0.5*1.62 rise=3
|meas tran pt1b when v(pro1)=0.5*1.62 rise=13
|let p_tr1 = (pt1b - pt1a)/10
|
|meas tran vsub_max MAX v(xarr.vsubs) from=100n to=800n
|meas tran vsub_min MIN v(xarr.vsubs) from=100n to=800n
|let vsub_swing_frac = (vsub_max - vsub_min) / 1.62
|
|print p_tr1
|print vsub_swing_frac
|.endc
|.end
|

